// The numeric half of a row, and the two structural questions about a type
// name: which row is it, and is it a list?

ty_row2(int tw, int ts) {
  push((import tywidth), tw);
  push((import tysigned), ts);
} return void;

// The row index of a type name, or -1. Every other lookup goes through here,
// so "type I have never heard of" has exactly one representation.
ty_find(string t) {
} return int find_str((import tyname), t);

// A list type is derived, not registered: `T[]` for any T. 93 is `]`. The
// length test rules out the empty string, whose last character does not exist.
ty_is_list(string t) {
  int ok = 0;
  if(len(t) > 2 && charat(t, len(t) - 1) == 93) {
    ok = 1;
  }
} return int ok;
